00:08:47.315 --> 00:08:49.497
- [Voiceover] Kat asks,
"How do you continue

00:08:49.497 --> 00:08:51.401
"kicking ass with work while going through

00:08:51.401 --> 00:08:53.746
"serious personal crisis?

00:08:53.746 --> 00:08:56.138
"How do you separate yet deal with both?"

00:08:56.138 --> 00:08:57.252
- You know Kat, it's interesting.

00:08:57.252 --> 00:08:58.854
This is a tough question for me.

00:08:58.854 --> 00:09:03.568
I'm not so sold I really know the answer.

00:09:03.568 --> 00:09:05.100
One of the things I'm very curious about,

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.421
and I fancy myself in being very resilient

00:09:08.421 --> 00:09:10.650
and things of that nature,
but I'm very emotional.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:15.247
Going through a very,
very, how is it worded?

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:18.776
A person crisis,

00:09:18.776 --> 00:09:22.073
a serious personal crisis
for me could be enough

00:09:22.073 --> 00:09:24.070
to put me in a position where I would

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.973
check out from a day to day hustle

00:09:26.973 --> 00:09:28.226
and business standpoint

00:09:28.226 --> 00:09:30.595
and really go address
that whether with myself

00:09:30.595 --> 00:09:32.499
or whatever I had to address.

00:09:32.499 --> 00:09:35.030
I often think about, knock on wood,

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.839
the bad things that are
conceivable in my life

00:09:37.839 --> 00:09:40.672
and how quickly everybody
around me will realize

00:09:40.672 --> 00:09:43.853
how little I give a crap about business

00:09:43.853 --> 00:09:45.525
in those moments.

00:09:45.525 --> 00:09:48.868
I've been outrageously fortunate,

00:09:48.868 --> 00:09:51.817
or unfortunate depending on
how you wanna look at it.

00:09:51.817 --> 00:09:54.975
I lost two of my grandparents long before

00:09:54.975 --> 00:09:56.345
I was born.

00:09:56.345 --> 00:09:58.945
I lost my mom's dad, my grandfather

00:09:58.945 --> 00:10:01.244
before he was able, a couple months

00:10:01.244 --> 00:10:03.171
before he was coming
to America to join us.

00:10:03.171 --> 00:10:04.866
I don't remember him.

00:10:04.866 --> 00:10:08.140
I've only had one grandparent growing up

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:12.061
which created a scenario where I haven't

00:10:12.061 --> 00:10:14.406
fortunately had a lot
of death or sickness.

00:10:14.406 --> 00:10:15.637
That's a cliche thing.

00:10:15.637 --> 00:10:18.261
Obviously so many of us, not me thank God,

00:10:18.261 --> 00:10:20.792
so many of you, so many people here

00:10:20.792 --> 00:10:22.696
have dealt with crisises
that are way more intense

00:10:22.696 --> 00:10:24.623
whether it's siblings or parents,

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:28.709
or uncles or aunts or best friends

00:10:28.709 --> 00:10:30.010
they're close to.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.099
I've been extremely fortunate.

00:10:32.099 --> 00:10:35.187
I think I'm driven by that gratitude.

00:10:35.187 --> 00:10:38.415
I think people are confused
by the gratitude I talk about.

00:10:38.415 --> 00:10:39.762
It's not the monies.

00:10:39.762 --> 00:10:43.987
It's, or the amazing audience

00:10:43.987 --> 00:10:47.215
and admiration I get from thousands.

00:10:47.215 --> 00:10:49.787
It is far more predicated on

00:10:50.117 --> 00:10:52.253
the health and wellbeing of my family

00:10:52.253 --> 00:10:53.484
and dearest friends.

00:10:53.484 --> 00:10:57.989
I would say as somebody who pushes

00:10:57.989 --> 00:11:00.700
hustle 24/7 365,

00:11:01.077 --> 00:11:03.468
that that is probably
the area where I think

00:11:03.468 --> 00:11:06.162
outside of actually having to do it,

00:11:06.162 --> 00:11:07.578
to put food on your table,

00:11:07.578 --> 00:11:11.757
or stay practical, I
think that is absolutely

00:11:11.757 --> 00:11:13.638
the time and place and the permission

00:11:13.638 --> 00:11:17.794
to step away, regroup,
have time for yourself,

00:11:17.794 --> 00:11:18.886
deal with those issues,

00:11:18.886 --> 00:11:20.279
and come back fresh.

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:23.344
I think that it's a mental game,

00:11:23.344 --> 00:11:26.664
and it would be insane for me to sit here

00:11:26.664 --> 00:11:30.518
and impose a strategy without having all

00:11:30.518 --> 00:11:31.238
the context.

00:11:31.238 --> 00:11:32.306
I think it's different for everybody.

00:11:32.306 --> 00:11:34.466
I know a lot of people that go the reverse

00:11:34.466 --> 00:11:37.832
and go deep into their
work to shut it down.

00:11:37.832 --> 00:11:40.410
My intuition is I'm not that.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:44.125
My intuition and having
a lot of self-awareness

00:11:44.125 --> 00:11:45.959
is I check out a little bit,

00:11:45.959 --> 00:11:48.536
and I let all the
wonderful people that I've

00:11:48.536 --> 00:11:50.789
done a lot of good for as a leader

00:11:50.789 --> 00:11:53.064
step up in those days or weeks,

00:11:53.064 --> 00:11:57.360
or months, because I've
